WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.238
Unit 3 is reading the audit.

2
00:00:02.238 --> 00:00:06.088
Its most consequential output is
the Arc-eligibility category.

3
00:00:06.088 --> 00:00:08.813
Category 1 is ready for Entra logins now.

4
00:00:08.813 --> 00:00:13.412
Category 2 needs Arc deployed and
Entra authentication configured first.

5
00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:16.637
Within it, instances with
many Windows logins,

6
00:00:16.637 --> 00:00:19.862
active SQL logins or
missing S P Ns go first.

7
00:00:19.862 --> 00:00:25.424
Category 3 is a version before SQL Server
2022, or a failover cluster instance

8
00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:30.238
on any version, and must upgrade,
re-platform or carry a dated exception.

9
00:00:30.238 --> 00:00:34.965
Engine Entra authentication, Layer
1, proceeds on a domain-joined host,

10
00:00:34.965 --> 00:00:38.225
and never waits for O S
level Entra sign-in, Layer 2.

11
00:00:38.225 --> 00:00:41.525
The kit settles only the first pass here,

12
00:00:41.525 --> 00:00:45.125
Category 3 or "1 or 2";
Module 3 settles the rest.

13
00:00:45.125 --> 00:00:48.300
And the audit names the engine's
service account and stops.

14
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:52.730
Converting a user account used as a service
belongs to the service account guide.
